[0.015,"o","\u001b[5;1H\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\nEnglish | [\u001b[38;5;12m\u001b[48;5;1m日本語\u001b[m](\u001b[38;5;13mREADME-ja.md\u001b[m)\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\nRun a YAML \u001b[38;5;15m**scenario** \u001b[mand record a terminal scene take [\u001b[38;5;12m\u001b[48;5;1masciinema v3 \u001b[38;5;9m\u001b[49m`\u001b[m.cast\u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[m](\u001b[38;5;13mhttps://docs.asciinema.org/manual/asciicast/v3/\u001b[m), animated \u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[m.svg\u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[m. You do not need to install or launch \u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[masciinema\u001b[38;5;9m` \u001b[mto record. Write a YAML scenario with steps, and this tool executes those steps and records the output as \u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[m.cast\u001b[38;5;9m` \u001b[m(and optionally \u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[m.svg\u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[m)—ordinary steps get simulated typing; steps with \u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[mpty: true\u001b[38;5;9m` \u001b[mcapture the terminal stream in real time.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\nSample scenario \u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[msamples/basic.yaml\u001b[38;5;9m` \u001b[mgenerates \u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[m.cast\u001b[38;5;9m` \u001b[mand \u001b[38;5;9m`\u001b[m.svg\u001b[38;5;9m` \u001b[moutput like below. You don't have to struggle with typing, and since the commands are actually executed, you can easily create realistic terminal recordings.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;9m\r\n```yaml\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\ntitle: \"Basic Demo\"\u001b[K\r\nwidth: 80\u001b[K\r\nheight: 24\u001b[K\u001b[24;53H  \u001b[8C5,0-1         Top \u001b[6;1H\u001b[?25h"]
